      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Leonard Wilson Keenan Estate & Letting Agents. Our business is you.\r\n\r\nSUBSTANTIAL 5 BED 2 BATH & 1 WC  SEMI-DETACHED FAMILY HOME\r\n\r\nPERFECT FOR RENOVATION\r\n\r\nSITUATED ON THE HIGHLY SOUGHT AFTER SHANLISS ROAD \r\n\r\nSOUTH FACING BACK GARDEN\r\n\r\nEARLY VIEWING STRONGLY ADVISED\r\n\r\nDesmond Keany and The Leonard Wilson Keenan team are delighted to present this lovely family home to the D9 property market.\r\n\r\nShanliss Road  is a very popular residential area, This property is sure to appeal to a diverse range of buyers.\r\n\r\nOn approach to Number 74 you will note the quality cobble lock driveway with ample off street parking and distinctive red brick facade with attractive bow windows. \r\n\r\nOn entering ,the ground floor of the property consists of a large welcoming entrance hallway with feature stained glass door panels, off which you have a large sitting room with a feature fireplace and attractive coving & mouldings , the good sized dining room is accessed through glazed doors . \r\n\r\nThe large kitchen is conveniently located off the Dining room, in addition ,behind the kitchen you will find a large pantry / utility room, and then  leading back to the entrance hallway you will note a  large study, or additional bedroom. There is a sun room of timber construction to the rear of the property overlooking a generous cobble lock  courtyard garden with bedding  ,  there is a WC and storage press off the sun room. Across the courtyard you will note a large block built shed extending the width of the property, the roof is pitched &  tiled and has two Velux windows, this structure may suit a number of uses. \r\n\r\n\r\nUpstairs boasts 4 bedrooms,three of which are double and one large single  one of which is ensuite and has a compact walk-in wardrobe , the other two doubles , including the principal bedroom have built-in wardrobes. There is a large airing cupboard and  a family bathroom completing the first floor.\r\n\r\nThe floored attic conversion offers additional space and potential.  \r\n\r\nWith excellent bus routes providing easy access to the city center, and an array of amenities including shops, cafes, parks ( Botanic Gardens , Albert College Park & Tolka Park) , churches, recreational facilities, and sports clubs within walking distance, this property offers both convenience and tranquility. Furthermore, it falls within the catchment area of esteemed primary and secondary schools, with DCU just a 10-minute stroll away. The omni shopping center and gulliver park are also close by, ensuring all your needs are met. Easy access to Dublin Airport and M50 , the proposed Metro will be near at hand also when completed.\r\n\r\n74 Shanliss road offers a unique blend of convenience and potential. Its strategic location near DCU makes it an attractive option for a variety of buyers, from families to investors. \r\n\r\nEarly viewing is strongly advised.\r\n \r\n***All information provided is to the best of our knowledge. The utmost of care and attention has been placed on providing factual and correct information. In certain cases some information may have been provided by the vendor to us. We do not hold any responsibility for mistakes, errors or inaccuracies in our online advertising and give each and every viewer the right to get an opinion on any concern they may have***"
      },
